 "slug": "3-introduction",
 "title": "Introduction",
 "content": "<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><body><div data-type=\"page\" id=\"page_b56f3f62-f26d-4a04-a9fd-dd9bb6e23fda\" class=\"introduction\" data-book-content=\"true\"><div class=\"os-figure has-splash\"><figure id=\"CNX_Calc_Figure_03_00_001\" class=\"splash\">\n<span data-type=\"media\" id=\"fs-id1169738055591\" data-alt=\"A photo of a Hennessey Venom GT sports car speeding along a winding road.\">\n<img src=\"../resources/5cc74a5a21e5ffc8bf7fcad876566fb0a34b498a\" data-media-type=\"image/jpeg\" alt=\"A photo of a Hennessey Venom GT sports car speeding along a winding road.\" width=\"975\" height=\"650\" />\n</span>\n\n</figure><div class=\"os-caption-container\">\n  <span class=\"os-title-label\">Figure </span>\n<span class=\"os-number\">3.1</span>\n\n\n\n  <span class=\"os-divider\"> </span>\n  <span class=\"os-caption\">The Hennessey Venom GT can go from 0 to 200 mph in 14.51 seconds. (credit: modification of work by Codex41, Flickr)</span>\n</div></div>\n\n\n\n\n  \n  \n  <div class=\"intro-body\">\n  <div class=\"os-chapter-outline\">\n  <h2 class=\"os-title\">Chapter Outline</h2>\n  <ul class=\"os-chapter-objectives\"><li class=\"os-chapter-objective\">\n  <a class=\"os-chapter-objective\" href=\"./8b89d172-2927-466f-8661-01abc7ccdba4@8dbc2ce:874f263f-c81b-42ff-9d4f-0fc8db63974c.xhtml\" aria-label=\"Go to Section 3.1 Defining the Derivative\" data-page-slug=\"3-1-defining-the-derivative\" data-page-uuid=\"874f263f-c81b-42ff-9d4f-0fc8db63974c\" data-page-fragment=\"\">\n    <span class=\"os-number\">3.1</span>\n    <span class=\"os-divider\"> </span>\n    <span data-type=\"\" itemprop=\"\" class=\"os-text\">Defining the Derivative</span>\n  </a>\n</li>\n<li class=\"os-chapter-objective\">\n  <a class=\"os-chapter-objective\" href=\"./8b89d172-2927-466f-8661-01abc7ccdba4@8dbc2ce:272d1a59-5e99-4a80-90e1-ccf60fb3cc1c.xhtml\" aria-label=\"Go to Section 3.2 The Derivative as a Function\" data-page-slug=\"3-2-the-derivative-as-a-function\" data-page-uuid=\"272d1a59-5e99-4a80-90e1-ccf60fb3cc1c\" data-page-fragment=\"\">\n    <span class=\"os-number\">3.2</span>\n    <span class=\"os-divider\"> </span>\n    <span data-type=\"\" itemprop=\"\" class=\"os-text\">The Derivative as a Function</span>\n  </a>\n</li>\n<li class=\"os-chapter-objective\">\n  <a class=\"os-chapter-objective\" href=\"./8b89d172-2927-466f-8661-01abc7ccdba4@8dbc2ce:f1a25413-3af2-4f97-8aac-dd75a16c8aea.xhtml\" aria-label=\"Go to Section 3.3 Differentiation Rules\" data-page-slug=\"3-3-differentiation-rules\" data-page-uuid=\"f1a25413-3af2-4f97-8aac-dd75a16c8aea\" data-page-fragment=\"\">\n    <span class=\"os-number\">3.3</span>\n    <span class=\"os-divider\"> </span>\n    <span data-type=\"\" itemprop=\"\" class=\"os-text\">Differentiation Rules</span>\n  </a>\n</li>\n<li class=\"os-chapter-objective\">\n  <a class=\"os-chapter-objective\" href=\"./8b89d172-2927-466f-8661-01abc7ccdba4@8dbc2ce:610ace30-270f-4dfc-8fad-5e44c4723919.xhtml\" aria-label=\"Go to Section 3.4 Derivatives as Rates of Change\" data-page-slug=\"3-4-derivatives-as-rates-of-change\" data-page-uuid=\"610ace30-270f-4dfc-8fad-5e44c4723919\" data-page-fragment=\"\">\n    <span class=\"os-number\">3.4</span>\n    <span class=\"os-divider\"> </span>\n    <span data-type=\"\" itemprop=\"\" class=\"os-text\">Derivatives as Rates of Change</span>\n  </a>\n</li>\n<li class=\"os-chapter-objective\">\n  <a class=\"os-chapter-objective\" href=\"./8b89d172-2927-466f-8661-01abc7ccdba4@8dbc2ce:147ddf25-f9d0-479f-be13-eab353ffee90.xhtml\" aria-label=\"Go to Section 3.5 Derivatives of Trigonometric Functions\" data-page-slug=\"3-5-derivatives-of-trigonometric-functions\" data-page-uuid=\"147ddf25-f9d0-479f-be13-eab353ffee90\" data-page-fragment=\"\">\n    <span class=\"os-number\">3.5</span>\n    <span class=\"os-divider\"> </span>\n    <span data-type=\"\" itemprop=\"\" class=\"os-text\">Derivatives of Trigonometric Functions</span>\n  </a>\n</li>\n<li class=\"os-chapter-objective\">\n  <a class=\"os-chapter-objective\" href=\"./8b89d172-2927-466f-8661-01abc7ccdba4@8dbc2ce:ec67b972-681d-403b-b456-82729dae0b91.xhtml\" aria-label=\"Go to Section 3.6 The Chain Rule\" data-page-slug=\"3-6-the-chain-rule\" data-page-uuid=\"ec67b972-681d-403b-b456-82729dae0b91\" data-page-fragment=\"\">\n    <span class=\"os-number\">3.6</span>\n    <span class=\"os-divider\"> </span>\n    <span data-type=\"\" itemprop=\"\" class=\"os-text\">The Chain Rule</span>\n  </a>\n</li>\n<li class=\"os-chapter-objective\">\n  <a class=\"os-chapter-objective\" href=\"./8b89d172-2927-466f-8661-01abc7ccdba4@8dbc2ce:afb02c92-f502-4a0f-91cf-793930632bd6.xhtml\" aria-label=\"Go to Section 3.7 Derivatives of Inverse Functions\" data-page-slug=\"3-7-derivatives-of-inverse-functions\" data-page-uuid=\"afb02c92-f502-4a0f-91cf-793930632bd6\" data-page-fragment=\"\">\n    <span class=\"os-number\">3.7</span>\n    <span class=\"os-divider\"> </span>\n    <span data-type=\"\" itemprop=\"\" class=\"os-text\">Derivatives of Inverse Functions</span>\n  </a>\n</li>\n<li class=\"os-chapter-objective\">\n  <a class=\"os-chapter-objective\" href=\"./8b89d172-2927-466f-8661-01abc7ccdba4@8dbc2ce:19fcb009-6677-4691-bf1a-a8d40e32bf11.xhtml\" aria-label=\"Go to Section 3.8 Implicit Differentiation\" data-page-slug=\"3-8-implicit-differentiation\" data-page-uuid=\"19fcb009-6677-4691-bf1a-a8d40e32bf11\" data-page-fragment=\"\">\n    <span class=\"os-number\">3.8</span>\n    <span class=\"os-divider\"> </span>\n    <span data-type=\"\" itemprop=\"\" class=\"os-text\">Implicit Differentiation</span>\n  </a>\n</li>\n<li class=\"os-chapter-objective\">\n  <a class=\"os-chapter-objective\" href=\"./8b89d172-2927-466f-8661-01abc7ccdba4@8dbc2ce:40fef24a-e790-49bf-9c6a-edc93696b724.xhtml\" aria-label=\"Go to Section 3.9 Derivatives of Exponential and Logarithmic Functions\" data-page-slug=\"3-9-derivatives-of-exponential-and-logarithmic-functions\" data-page-uuid=\"40fef24a-e790-49bf-9c6a-edc93696b724\" data-page-fragment=\"\">\n    <span class=\"os-number\">3.9</span>\n    <span class=\"os-divider\"> </span>\n    <span data-type=\"\" itemprop=\"\" class=\"os-text\">Derivatives of Exponential and Logarithmic Functions</span>\n  </a>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n  <div class=\"intro-text\">\n    <h2 data-type=\"document-title\" id=\"page_b56f3f62-f26d-4a04-a9fd-dd9bb6e23fda_titlecreatedbycookbook\" data-rex-keep=\"true\"><span data-type=\"\" itemprop=\"\" class=\"os-text\">Introduction</span>\n</h2>\n    <p id=\"fs-id1169737736796\">The Hennessey Venom GT is one of the fastest cars in the world. In 2014, it reached a record-setting speed of 270.49 mph. It can go from 0 to 200 mph in 14.51 seconds. The techniques in this chapter can be used to calculate the acceleration the Venom achieves in this feat (see <a href=\"./8b89d172-2927-466f-8661-01abc7ccdba4@8dbc2ce:874f263f-c81b-42ff-9d4f-0fc8db63974c.xhtml#fs-id1169739204154\" class=\"autogenerated-content\" aria-label=\"Go to Example 3.8\" data-page-slug=\"3-1-defining-the-derivative\" data-page-uuid=\"874f263f-c81b-42ff-9d4f-0fc8db63974c\" data-page-fragment=\"fs-id1169739204154\">Example 3.8</a>.)</p><p id=\"fs-id1169738017022\">Calculating velocity and changes in velocity are important uses of calculus, but it is far more widespread than that. Calculus is important in all branches of mathematics, science, and engineering, and it is critical to analysis in business and health as well. In this chapter, we explore one of the main tools of calculus, the derivative, and show convenient ways to calculate derivatives. We apply these rules to a variety of functions in this chapter so that we can then explore applications of these techniques.</p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n</div></body></html>"
}